    "summary": "Equal masses hang from two identical rods. The left joint breaks above 3 N, which is less than the hanging weight. The right joint can hold 20 N and stays connected. A broken link appears as grey torn ends, and its mass falls freely.",
    "title": "When a joint breaks"
  },
