  "guide": {"focus":"The rods carry equal masses. Compare what happens when their joints have different breaking limits.","predict":{"prompt":"Which link breaks first when gravity is increased?","options":["Weak left link","Strong right link","Both together"]},"variables":[{"control":"world.gravity.strength","label":"Gravity strength"}],"steps":[{"text":"Reduce gravity, press R, then increase it.","control":"world.gravity.strength"},{"text":"Press Play and watch the weak link break when its load passes the limit."},{"text":"Press R to replay the break and compare the graph.","open":"measure.graph"}],"expect":"The left link holds below 3 N and breaks above it. The right link keeps holding until its load exceeds 20 N.","limits":"A broken joint stays broken for the rest of the run. Back to start restores it so you can try again."},
